From: SF2000 Linux project
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: hc15: accept post-data STOP latch completion

Physical SF2000 traces show a successful multi-block transfer followed by a
CMD12 timeout and card re-enumeration.  Unlike ordinary response commands, the
HC15xx post-data STOP path does not raise a second command IRQ: it completes by
clearing CMDCTL.start.  hc15_wait_irq already supports this vendor completion
contract for data commands.  Enable it for the STOP command as well; response
and terminal-status validation still run normally afterward.

---
 drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c b/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c
--- a/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/hc15_mmc.c
@@ -1045,7 +1045,7 @@ done:
 		hc15_mark("hc15-stop-entry", mrq->stop->opcode);
 		hc15_set_command(host, mrq->stop, NULL);
 		hc15_start_command(host);
-		hc15_wait_irq(host, mrq->stop, false);
+		hc15_wait_irq(host, mrq->stop, true);
 		hc15_get_response(host, mrq->stop);
 		hc15_mark("hc15-stop-error", mrq->stop->error);
 		hc15_mark("hc15-stop-resp0", mrq->stop->resp[0]);
-- 
2.0.0
